        <summary type="html"><![CDATA[What is MeteoStack?]]></summary>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="what-is-meteostack">What is MeteoStack?<a href="https://meteostack.org/blog/welcome-to-meteostack/#what-is-meteostack" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to What is MeteoStack?" title="Direct link to What is MeteoStack?" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>MeteoStack is an open-source project designed help people collect weather data
using a custom self-built weather station.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th><img src="https://meteostack.org/img/MeteoStack.png" width="256" height="256"></th><th><video width="320" height="240" loop="" autoplay=""><source src="/img/loading.webm" type="video/webm"></video></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Logo</td><td>Loading animation</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>(Credit for the logo design: <a class="" href="https://meteostack.org/blog/authors/samma-2009/">Samma2009</a>)</p>
<!-- -->
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="community-driven">Community-driven<a href="https://meteostack.org/blog/welcome-to-meteostack/#community-driven" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Community-driven" title="Direct link to Community-driven" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>I intend this to be a community-driven project, and the community will be involved
throughout every decision possible, polls will be held when making decisions, so
watch out for them, as that's how you can help choose what happens with the project!</p>
<p>If you would like to join in on the decision making, please either join the
<a href="https://go.wtdawson.info/ms-ds/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="">Discord server</a>, and or the
<a href="https://go.wtdawson.info/ms-sc/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="">Serchat server</a>. This is where polls are linked to,
and where you can receive the latest news and announcements.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="little-to-no-reliance-on-third-party-dependencies">Little-to-no reliance on third-party dependencies<a href="https://meteostack.org/blog/welcome-to-meteostack/#little-to-no-reliance-on-third-party-dependencies" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Little-to-no reliance on third-party dependencies" title="Direct link to Little-to-no reliance on third-party dependencies" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>MeteoStack will run on its own libraries where possible, to minimise the reliance on third-party dependencies,
this is so that it's easier to manage, to update, but also for security, and for the overall quality of the software.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="more-to-come-soon">More to come soon...<a href="https://meteostack.org/blog/welcome-to-meteostack/#more-to-come-soon" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to More to come soon..." title="Direct link to More to come soon..." translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>Future blog posts may be released detailing more about the project, how you can get involved, and how you can use
the project to build your own weather station.</p>]]></content>
